* History of thoracic or back surgery with suspected damage to the thoracodorsal vessels;
* Poor general condition and inability to tolerate surgery;
* Presence of severe comorbidities, such as uncontrolled diabetes, severe bone marrow suppression after breast cancer treatment, compromised immune function, or a history of long-term smoking;
